# LIMIT — Completion Relevance Record

Date: 2026-08-25

## 1 — Source

`limit` is a native read-only executable inventory utility. It consumes executable metadata and binary identity information without modifying the inspected filesystem.

## 2 — Compiler relationship

The preferred build compiler is the repository-derived GCC 16.2.0 toolchain. When the MEARVK metadata contract is available, `limit` is built with explicit provenance metadata describing edition, version, company, source, and build context.

## 3 — Verification

The source-level integration is complete. Actual emitted `MEARVK-META` records remain subject to local GCC bootstrap/build verification.

## 4 — Production status

The source, build contract, README, HSS, HSSS, and production record are maintained together. Unrelated working-tree changes are not staged by the GCC/tool build process.